# Environment variables these skills read. Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill
# in, or export directly in the shell/session that runs Claude Science.
#
# None of these variables has a built-in default: each skill raises
# FileNotFoundError naming the variable when it is unset, rather than
# silently trying a path from the machine they were developed on. See
# README.md "Running these on another Claude Science account" for what each
# points at and why it can't be scripted (depmap.org and the trained GeneTEA
# model are both manual downloads).

# Directory holding the local DepMap release: CRISPRGeneEffect.csv, Model.csv,
# CRISPRGeneDependency.csv, and the other files depmap-local/README.md lists.
# Required by: depmap-local, depmap-genetea.
DEPMAP_ROOT=

# Path to a trained GeneTEA.pkl (1.11 GB). Required by: depmap-genetea only.
# Source: https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.28635317, file 53289398.
GENETEA_MODEL=

# This repo's results/ directory - where every skill's run-output writer
# (fusion_run_dir, kba_run_dir, genetea_run_dir, mcn_run_dir, gps_run_dir,
# brief_run_dir, audit_run_dir) saves a run. No cwd-relative default: each
# raises FileNotFoundError naming this variable when it is unset, rather than
# silently creating a new "results/" folder wherever the kernel session's
# working directory happens to be. Required by: target-lit-brief,
# boltz-affinity-triage, depmap-fusion, depmap-genetea, get-protein-structure,
# marker-contrast-null, ai-origination-audit. Point it at this repo's own
# results/ directory, e.g. /path/to/claude_science_targets/results.
SCIENCE_RESULTS_ROOT=
